{"content":[{"c":["BANKER, BANKING"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["A person who engages in loaning, exchanging, and issuing money. The development of interstate and international trade made it imperative to devise a method of banking to facilitate the transfer of funds. The appearance of coinage in the seventh century ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"}," brought the money changer into being. The royal monopoly in commerce (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.5.11","r":"2Sam.5.11","rawR":"2Sam.5.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.5.11","value":"2Sam.5.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 5:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.10.14-29","r":"1Kgs.10.14-29","rawR":"1Kgs.10.14-29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.10.14-29","value":"1Kgs.10.14-29"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 10:14-29"},") gave place to a system that resembled modern banking."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["In NT times money changers represented one aspect of the banking system. They spent their time converting Roman money into orthodox coinage for the temple half-shekel (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.17.24","r":"Matt.17.24","rawR":"Matt.17.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.17.24","value":"Matt.17.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 17:24"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.21.12","r":"Matt.21.12","rawR":"Matt.21.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.21.12","value":"Matt.21.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"21:12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.25.27","r":"Matt.25.27","rawR":"Matt.25.27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.25.27","value":"Matt.25.27"}],"t":"ref","v":"25:27"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.11.15","r":"Mark.11.15","rawR":"Mark.11.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.11.15","value":"Mark.11.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mk 11:15"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.19.23","r":"Luke.19.23","rawR":"Luke.19.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.19.23","value":"Luke.19.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 19:23"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=John.2.14-15","r":"John.2.14-15","rawR":"John.2.14-15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.2.14-15","value":"John.2.14-15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jn 2:14-15"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["Those who lent money (lenders) and those who gave credit in financial transactions (creditors) were protected by a system of guarantees such as pieces of movable property or a pledge of some kind. Interest was theoretically forbidden by Israelite law (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.22.25","r":"Exod.22.25","rawR":"Exod.22.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.22.25","value":"Exod.22.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 22:25"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.15.1-18","r":"Deut.15.1-18","rawR":"Deut.15.1-18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.15.1-18","value":"Deut.15.1-18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 15:1-18"},"), although the law was not always observed and exorbitant rates of interest were sometimes charged. Prophets and some national leaders deplored the practice (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.5.6-13","r":"Neh.5.6-13","rawR":"Neh.5.6-13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.5.6-13","value":"Neh.5.6-13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 5:6-13"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.18.8,13,17","r":"Ezek.18.8,13,17","rawR":"Ezek.18.8,13,17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.18.8,13,17","value":"Ezek.18.8,13,17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 18:8, 13, 17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.22.12","r":"Ezek.22.12","rawR":"Ezek.22.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.22.12","value":"Ezek.22.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"22:12"},"). Often, the people of Israel were afraid of their creditors (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.4.1","r":"2Kgs.4.1","rawR":"2Kgs.4.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.4.1","value":"2Kgs.4.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 4:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.109.11","r":"Ps.109.11","rawR":"Ps.109.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.109.11","value":"Ps.109.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 109:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.24.2","r":"Isa.24.2","rawR":"Isa.24.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.24.2","value":"Isa.24.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 24:2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.50.1","r":"Isa.50.1","rawR":"Isa.50.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.50.1","value":"Isa.50.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"50:1"},"), who might invade their homes to recover a debt, even carrying off children as slaves (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.4.1","r":"2Kgs.4.1","rawR":"2Kgs.4.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.4.1","value":"2Kgs.4.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 4:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.50.1","r":"Isa.50.1","rawR":"Isa.50.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.50.1","value":"Isa.50.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 50:1"},"). The parable of the creditor and the two debtors in ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.7.41-42","r":"Luke.7.41-42","rawR":"Luke.7.41-42","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.7.41-42","value":"Luke.7.41-42"}],"t":"ref","v":"Luke 7:41-42"}," represents a kindly creditor (cf. ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.25.14-30","r":"Matt.25.14-30","rawR":"Matt.25.14-30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.25.14-30","value":"Matt.25.14-30"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 25:14-30"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.19.11-27","r":"Luke.19.11-27","rawR":"Luke.19.11-27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.19.11-27","value":"Luke.19.11-27"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 19:11-27"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Money_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Money_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Money_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Money"},"; ",{"href":"?item=MoneyChanger_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"MoneyChanger_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"MoneyChanger_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Money Changer"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"BankerBanking","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Sm 5:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.5.11","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.5.11","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.5.11"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 10:14-29","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.10.14-29","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.10.14-29","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.10.14-29"},{"anchorText":"Mt 17:24","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.17.24","rawQueryValue"